#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:10004
msgid "Working with the `Parameters` Class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:10006
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Gal3D` uses the {py:class}`Parameters "
"<gal3d.optimization.parameter.Parameters>` class to manage and store "
"model parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:20002
msgid "Basic Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:30002
msgid "We can define a set of parameters as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:40002
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{array}{r c l}\n"
"\\mathbf{Parameters} & & \\\\\n"
"\\mathrm{a} & : & 3.000 \\in [-\\infty, \\infty] \\\\\n"
"\\mathrm{b} & : & 2.000 \\in [-\\infty, \\infty] \\\\\n"
"\\mathrm{c} & : & 1.000 \\in [-\\infty, \\infty]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:50002
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each parameter value is represented by a {py:class}`Parameter "
"<gal3d.optimization.parameter.Parameter>` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:50004
msgid ""
"The lower bound (`lb`) and upper bound (`ub`) of each parameter can be "
"specified explicitly. If they are not given, they default to negative "
"infinity and positive infinity, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:60002
msgid "3.000 \\in [-\\infty, \\infty]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:70002
msgid "You can modify `lb` and `ub` directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:90002
msgid "You can also set bounds in batch using the `set_ub` and `set_lb` methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:110002
msgid "Adding Extra Information and Derived Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:110004
msgid ""
"You can add derived parameters using the `add_derived` method. The names "
"of all derived parameters can be obtained with `derived_keys`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:130002
msgid ""
"You can add additional information using the `add_info` method. The names"
" of all such entries can be obtained with `info_keys`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:150002
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The list of basic parameter names can be obtained using `parameter_keys`."
" These are all {py:class}`Parameter "
"<gal3d.optimization.parameter.Parameter>` objects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:170002
msgid "Adding Parameter Constraints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:170004
msgid ""
"You can add equality constraints to basic parameters using the "
"`add_equal_constraints` method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:190002
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{array}{r c l}\n"
"\\mathbf{Parameters} & & \\\\\n"
"\\mathrm{a} & : & 3.000 \\in [0.300, \\infty] \\\\\n"
"\\mathrm{b} & : & 2.000 \\in [0.200, \\infty] \\\\\n"
"\\mathrm{c} & : & \\lgroup 2.000,\\ \\mathrm{constraint} \\rgroup\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:200002
msgid "Parameters with equality constraints are removed from `parameter_keys`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:220002
msgid ""
"You can remove previously added equality constraints using the "
"`del_equal_constraints` method. The corresponding parameters will then "
"reappear in `parameter_keys` and return to their original unconstrained "
"state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:240002
msgid "Parameter Priority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:240004
msgid ""
"In the `Parameters` class, values are divided into basic parameters, "
"constrained parameters, derived parameters, and additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:240006
msgid "Their priority, from highest to lowest, is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:240008
msgid ""
"constrained parameters > basic parameters > derived parameters > "
"additional information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/parameters.ipynb:240010
msgid ""
"That is, when retrieving a value, `Parameters` searches in "
"`constraint_keys`, `parameter_keys`, `derived_keys`, and `info_keys` in "
"that order."
msgstr ""

